work_units.notes:
Add or update tests so CI fails when:
  - `set(ascii_runtime._CHART_TYPE_DISPATCH) != set(ALL_CHART_TYPES)`;
  - templates reference an unregistered chart;
  - MCP chart descriptions are missing any registered chart;
  - Results Explorer `ALL_CHART_IDS` diverges from the Python registry;
  - discovery metadata claims a stale chart subset without documenting it
    as intentionally partial.

The test should distinguish required coverage from intentionally partial
surfaces. For example, discovery metadata may be allowed to expose a short
"common chart types" list only if the code names it as partial and links
to the full registry.

Add concise documentation near the registry or in
`docs/reference/public-contracts.md` explaining:
  - semantic result-aware chart IDs vs raw textcharts primitive IDs;
  - which chart IDs are public CLI/MCP/Explorer contracts;
  - what files/tests must change for a new chart type;
  - whether `render_ascii_chart` is supported, deprecated, or internal;
  - how textcharts dependency updates are validated.
